 "sources": {
  "clock_meridiem_night": [
   "The NIGHT daypart is a midnight-crossing BAND in colloquial clock usage,",
   "not a uniform +12 PM shift: \"la una de la nueche\" is 01:00, \"les diez de",
   "la nueche\" is 22:00, twelve is midnight 00:00.  Small hours 1..5 stay AM,",
   "evening hours 6..11 are PM, twelve is midnight (band-split in resolver",
   "_clock_hms).  AST is Ibero-Romance and shares the same madrugada band",
   "[00:00, 06:00) as es/ca/pt (chronologia/dayparts.py); the 5|6 cut is",
   "inherited from the RAE/DIEC/Priberam-cited boundary for the sibling",
   "Ibero-Romance locales (see chronologia/locale/es/clock_meridiem_night.voc)",
   "pending native confirmation for Asturian (tracked in issue #266)."
  ],
  "daypart_morning": [
   "\"la mañana\" is the morning: DALLA s.v. \"mañana, la\": \"Parte [del día] que va",
   "dende l'amanecida hasta'l meudía.\"  The adverb \"mañana\" is tomorrow (DALLA",
   "s.v. \"mañana\": \"Nel día que sigue al de güei\"), so the morning reading needs",
   "a demonstrative, an article, \"de\" (DALLA: \"|| De mañana, na parte del día que",
   "va dende l'amanecida hasta'l meudía\") or \"pela\" before it.  No CLDR",
   "day-period rules exist for ast; the band is the library default morning,",
   "[06:00, 12:00)."
  ],
  "marker_at_counts": [
   "Clock prepositions that also introduce a counted group: a bare hour behind one",
   "is doubtful only right before a word of marker_counted_noun.voc.  Attested in",
   "the parity acceptance rows; no dictionary source checked, a native reviewer is to confirm."
  ],
  "marker_counted_noun": [
   "Nouns that count people or things a clock never takes: a bare hour behind a",
   "clock preposition and directly before one of them is a count (\"wave at 5",
   "people\").  Each word is quoted from its Wiktionary Noun entry",
   "(https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/<word>); the fetched pages are kept with the audit.",
   "persona: Noun. \"person\"",
   "persones: Noun. \"plural of persona\"",
   "neños: Noun. \"plural of neñu\"",
   "neñes: Noun. \"plural of neña\"",
   "amigos: Noun. \"form of amigu\"",
   "amigues: Noun. \"plural of amiga\"",
   "rapazos: Noun. \"plural of rapaz\"",
   "xugadores: Noun. \"plural of xugador\"",
   "asientos: Noun. \"plural of asientu\"",
   "cuartos: Noun. \"plural of cuartu\""
  ],
  "marker_day_early": [
   "A day word followed by \"ceo\" names the first hours of that day: \"mañana",
   "ceo\" is tomorrow morning.  DALLA s.v. \"ceo\": \"Nes primeres hores del día.",
   "Los periódicos repártense ceo.\"  Without a day word it names no date."
  ],
  "marker_dayframe": [
   "\"per\" with the article frames a part of the day.  DALLA s.v. \"per\":",
   "\"allugamientu nel tiempu: Vémonos pela mañana\"; s.v. \"pel, pela, pelo\":",
   "\"contr. de la preposición per y l'artículu\"."
  ],
  "marker_daypart_after_day": [
   "\"de\" opens the morning only right after a day: \"el llunes de mañana\",",
   "\"mañana de mañana\".  DALLA lists \"De mañana, na parte del día que va dende",
   "l'amanecida hasta'l meudía\" (s.v. \"mañana, la\").  The adverb \"mañana\" is",
   "\"Nel día que sigue al de güei\" (s.v. \"mañana\"), and that is its reading in",
   "\"a partir de mañana\" and \"el día de mañana\": tomorrow."
  ],
  "marker_past": [
   "\"atrás\" closing a counted length is the postposed past marker, beside the",
   "preposed \"hai\"/\"fai\": ast.wikipedia has \"10,000 años atrás\" (Pleistocenu),",
   "\"sieglos atrás\" (Malí) and \"meses atrás\" (Israel).  Portuguese lists the",
   "same pair in this file."
  ],
  "marker_sharp": [
   "The exact hour, trailing the clock: DALLA s.v. \"puntu\", \"|| En puntu, a la",
   "hora exauta. 2 Exauta [una hora].\""
  ],
  "month_1": [
   "Unicode CLDR 47, locale ast, gregorian calendar (cldr-json",
   "cldr-dates-full/main/ast/ca-gregorian.json): months.stand-alone.wide,",
   "months.format.abbreviated, months.stand-alone.abbreviated."
  ],
  "month_10": [
   "Unicode CLDR 47, locale ast, gregorian calendar (cldr-json",
   "cldr-dates-full/main/ast/ca-gregorian.json): months.stand-alone.wide,",
   "months.format.abbreviated, months.stand-alone.abbreviated."
  ],
  "month_11": [
   "Unicode CLDR 47, locale ast, gregorian calendar (cldr-json",
   "cldr-dates-full/main/ast/ca-gregorian.json): months.stand-alone.wide.  Not",
   "covered by any of those charts, and so unattested here: \"noviembre\", \"nov\"."
  ],
  "month_12": [
   "Unicode CLDR 47, locale ast, gregorian calendar (cldr-json",
   "cldr-dates-full/main/ast/ca-gregorian.json): months.stand-alone.wide.  Not",
